SYNTHESIS
========================================================================================
1. A000568 appears exactly as the base of the observer-source cone.
2. LRC asks whether the arithmetic clock reaches that source-cone slice.
3. Raw moving-runner classes mix good and bad states, so projection is lossy.
4. THM-497 says scalar cover counts cannot prove LRC14; the missing data is
   alignment/fiber structure.  The source-deleted A000568 fiber is one such
   structural coordinate, while Q27/Q31 and blocking height are the LRC14
   multiplicative-cover coordinates.
5. New proof target: show that any long LRC14 blocked-band walk either enters
   a source-cone deleted class, or its failure to do so forces the balanced
   cover congruences feeding the Q31/7-ideal/13-clock portal.
